{
 "title": "Modeling basic objects: chair, treasure chest, grenade",
 "summary": "Three models from primitives with the editing tools. A chair: a cube flattened into a seat, six loop cuts each way, the corner faces underneath extruded into legs and spread, the back row of faces extruded up and leaned back, every other column bridged front to back (Bridge Edge Loops) into slats, bevelled, smooth shaded, brown. A treasure chest: a cube squashed into a box, the top extruded and narrowed into a lid, the four sides inset individually and pushed in along their normals (green panels), the lid's faces inset and pushed in (grey metal), its ends red, everything bevelled; a lock from two cubes, one extruded across and down into a shackle, joined and bevelled, blue. A grenade: a UV sphere (16 x 16) stretched, its poles deleted, the openings narrowed with proportional editing, every face extruded on its own into blocks, bevelled, the holes filled (F), the top extruded into a fuse, a lever extruded and rotated down the side; green, the lever grey metal (select linked), a yellow band.",
 "objects": [
